  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban climate action: pilot projects  under article 6 of the Paris Agreement in Indonesia &amp; Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cities cause over 40% of direct global CO2 emissions. However, mobilising significant emission reductions in cities is a major challenge due to the very heterogeneous urban structures. The project developed pragmatic approaches for the implementation of activities corresponding to Article 6 of the Paris Agreement in cities. In other words, the project pilots the integration of cities into the global emission trading system. A particular focus was on the involvement of relevant actors at the local, national level and international level. Furthermore, pragmatic structures and distribution mechanisms for Article 6 were conceptualised with the partners and relevant actors in the target countries. The expected outcome of the project was to have at least one pilot city in each country that is able to generate emission certificates according to Article 6.</narrative>
  </description>
